# Cursor Rules for Edna Take-Home Project

## Project Structure

This is a monorepo with two components:
- `data-pipeline/` - Dagster data pipeline (Python)
- `dashboard/` - Next.js dashboard (TypeScript)

## Data Pipeline (Python)

### Framework
- Dagster with `dg` CLI tooling
- Uses `@definitions` decorator pattern for assets
- One asset per file in `src/data_pipeline/defs/`

### Commands
```bash
cd data-pipeline
docker-compose up        # Run via Docker
uv sync                  # Install deps
.venv/bin/dg dev         # Run dev server
```

### Conventions
- Use Polars for DataFrame operations (not Pandas)
- Use PyArrow for Parquet I/O
- Parquet output must use `use_dictionary=False` for dashboard compatibility
- Assets write to `output/` directory

## Dashboard (TypeScript)

### Framework
- Next.js 16 with App Router
- React 19
- TypeScript strict mode

### Commands
```bash
cd dashboard
bun install
bun dev                  # Dev server on port 3001
bun run build
bun run lint
```

### Data Layer
- tRPC for API with React Query integration
- Routers in `server/routers/`
- Client hooks via `lib/trpc.ts`
- Parquet files read from `../data-pipeline/output/`

### UI Components
- shadcn/ui components in `components/ui/`
- Radix UI primitives
- Tailwind CSS v4
- Recharts for data visualization
- Use `cn()` utility from `lib/utils.ts` for className merging

### Parquet Compatibility
The dashboard uses `parquetjs-lite` which has limited encoding support. When writing Parquet from the data pipeline, always use:
```python
df.write_parquet(path, use_dictionary=False, version="1.0")
```

## FASTQ Data Format
```
@read_id          <- Header
ATCGATCG...       <- Sequence (A, T, C, G, N)
+                 <- Separator
IIIIII...         <- Quality scores (ASCII Phred: quality = ord(char) - 33)
```
- Q30 = 99.9% accuracy (error rate 1 in 1000)
- Q20 = 99% accuracy (error rate 1 in 100)

## Code Style

### TypeScript
- Prefer `interface` over `type` for object shapes
- Use React Server Components where possible
- Client components must have `"use client"` directive

### Python
- Use type hints
- Prefer Polars expressions over iterating rows
- Use pathlib for file paths
